@@ -265,6 +265,13 @@ WebSocket, and your application handles them with `onToolCall`. If the result is
 available immediately, return it from `onToolCall`. The SDK sends it back to the
 provider as tool output.
 
+On a turn-based connection where the SDK requests continuations, it waits for
+the response to complete and for all its tools to submit their outputs. New
+speech, a user submission, an explicit response request or cancellation, or a
+newer response supersedes that continuation. A late result still goes back
+with its original call ID. An application that wants the result announced
+later can invoke `requestResponse()` after the current reply.
+
 For server-backed tools, call an app-specific API endpoint from `onToolCall`.
 Avoid generic "execute tool by name" routes. App-specific endpoints are easier
 to secure because they can use your normal authentication, authorization,
